<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Recep Tayyip Erdoğan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Recep Tayyip Erdoğan is a Turkish politician who co-founded the Justice and Development Party (AKP) and has led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> since 2003, as prime minister until 2014 and then as president. A former mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>, he oversaw rapid economic growth in his first decade and opened accession talks with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>. After surviving a coup attempt in 2016 he introduced an executive presidency in 2018 and has governed in an increasingly authoritarian manner.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/recep-tayyip-erdogan.jpg" alt="Recep Tayyip Erdoğan" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rory Arnold · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkish_President_Recep_Tayyip_Erdo%C4%9Fan_in_January_2024_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
